    "content": "# Mechanics & Rotational Dynamics \u2014 High-Yield Formula Sheet\n*Curated by Nelov Mallick (IIT Delhi) \u00b7 Authentic JEE Advanced Revision*\n\n---\n\n## 1. Kinematics & Projectile Motion\n\n### 1.1 Standard Projectile on Level Ground\n- **Time of Flight:** $$T = \\frac{2u\\sin\\theta}{g} = \\frac{2u_y}{g}$$\n- **Maximum Height:** $$H_{\\max} = \\frac{u^2 \\sin^2\\theta}{2g} = \\frac{u_y^2}{2g}$$\n- **Horizontal Range:** $$R = \\frac{u^2 \\sin 2\\theta}{g} = \\frac{2 u_x u_y}{g}$$\n- **Trajectory Equation:**\n  $$y = x\\tan\\theta \\left(1 - \\frac{x}{R}\\right) = x\\tan\\theta - \\frac{g x^2}{2 u^2 \\cos^2\\theta}$$\n- **Radius of Curvature at Top:**\n  $$\\rho_{\\text{top}} = \\frac{v_{\\text{top}}^2}{a_\\perp} = \\frac{(u\\cos\\theta)^2}{g}$$\n\n### 1.2 Projectile on an Inclined Plane (Angle of incline $\\alpha$, projection angle $\\beta$ with incline)\n- **Time of Flight:** $$T = \\frac{2u\\sin\\beta}{g\\cos\\alpha}$$\n- **Range up the Incline:**\n  $$R_{\\text{up}} = \\frac{u^2}{g\\cos^2\\alpha}\\left[\\sin(2\\beta + \\alpha) - \\sin\\alpha\\right]$$\n- **Maximum Range Condition:** $$\\beta = \\frac{\\pi}{4} - \\frac{\\alpha}{2} \\implies R_{\\max} = \\frac{u^2}{g(1 + \\sin\\alpha)}$$\n\n---\n\n## 2. Newton's Laws & Friction\n\n- **Static Friction:** $$f_s \\le \\mu_s N$$ (self-adjusting force)\n- **Kinetic Friction:** $$f_k = \\mu_k N$$ (acts opposing relative surface velocity)\n- **Angle of Friction ($\\lambda$) & Repose ($\\theta_r$):**\n  $$\\tan\\lambda = \\mu_s, \\quad \\theta_r = \\lambda = \\arctan(\\mu_s)$$\n- **Conical Pendulum:**\n  $$T\\cos\\theta = mg, \\quad T\\sin\\theta = m\\omega^2 (L\\sin\\theta) \\implies \\omega = \\sqrt{\\frac{g}{L\\cos\\theta}}, \\quad \\text{Time Period } \\mathcal{T} = 2\\pi\\sqrt{\\frac{L\\cos\\theta}{g}}$$\n- **Banking of Tracks (without friction):**\n  $$\\tan\\theta = \\frac{v_0^2}{rg}$$\n- **Safe Speed Limits on Banked Curve with Friction:**\n  $$v_{\\min} = \\sqrt{rg \\left(\\frac{\\tan\\theta - \\mu}{1 + \\mu\\tan\\theta}\\right)}, \\quad v_{\\max} = \\sqrt{rg \\left(\\frac{\\tan\\theta + \\mu}{1 - \\mu\\tan\\theta}\\right)}$$\n\n---\n\n## 3. Work, Power & Energy\n\n- **Work Done by Variable Force:**\n  $$W = \\int_{\\vec{r}_1}^{\\vec{r}_2} \\vec{F}\\cdot d\\vec{r} = \\int (F_x dx + F_y dy + F_z dz)$$\n- **Conservative Force & Potential Energy:**\n  $$\\vec{F} = -\\nabla U = -\\left(\\frac{\\partial U}{\\partial x}\\hat{i} + \\frac{\\partial U}{\\partial y}\\hat{j} + \\frac{\\partial U}{\\partial z}\\hat{k}\\right)$$\n- **Equilibrium Criteria:**\n  - Stable Equilibrium: $\\frac{dU}{dx} = 0$ and $\\frac{d^2U}{dx^2} > 0$\n  - Unstable Equilibrium: $\\frac{dU}{dx} = 0$ and $\\frac{d^2U}{dx^2} < 0$\n  - Neutral Equilibrium: $\\frac{dU}{dx} = 0$ and $\\frac{d^2U}{dx^2} = 0$\n- **Work-Energy Theorem:**\n  $$W_{\\text{net}} = W_{\\text{conservative}} + W_{\\text{non-conservative}} + W_{\\text{external}} = \\Delta K$$\n- **Vertical Circular Motion (String of length $R$):**\n  - Minimum bottom velocity to complete loop: $$v_{\\text{bottom}} = \\sqrt{5gR}$$\n  - Minimum top velocity to maintain tautness: $$v_{\\text{top}} = \\sqrt{gR}$$\n  - Tension at bottom: $$T_{\\text{bottom}} = 6mg$$, Tension at top: $$T_{\\text{top}} = 0$$\n\n---\n\n## 4. Center of Mass & Collisions\n\n- **Center of Mass Coordinates:**\n  $$\\vec{r}_{cm} = \\frac{\\sum m_i \\vec{r}_i}{\\sum m_i} = \\frac{1}{M}\\int \\vec{r}\\,dm$$\n- **Truncated / Cavity Objects:**\n  $$\\vec{r}_{cm} = \\frac{M_1 \\vec{r}_1 - M_2 \\vec{r}_2}{M_1 - M_2}$$ (treating cavity as negative mass)\n- **Coefficient of Restitution ($e$):**\n  $$e = \\frac{\\text{Velocity of Separation along normal}}{\\text{Velocity of Approach along normal}} = \\frac{v_{2\\perp} - v_{1\\perp}}{u_{1\\perp} - u_{2\\perp}}$$\n  - $e = 1$: Perfectly elastic collision ($\\Delta K = 0$)\n  - $0 < e < 1$: Inelastic collision\n  - $e = 0$: Completely inelastic collision (bodies stick together)\n- **Energy Loss in 1D Collision:**\n  $$\\Delta K_{\\text{loss}} = \\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{m_1 m_2}{m_1 + m_2}\\right)(1 - e^2)(u_1 - u_2)^2$$\n\n---\n\n## 5. Rotational Dynamics & Moments of Inertia\n\n### 5.1 Fundamental Theorems\n- **Parallel Axis Theorem:** $$I = I_{cm} + M d^2$$ (valid for any rigid body; axes must be parallel and one must pass through CM)\n- **Perpendicular Axis Theorem:** $$I_z = I_x + I_y$$ (strictly valid for planar / 2D lamina only in the $xy$-plane)\n\n### 5.2 Key Moments of Inertia ($I_{cm}$)\n| Object | Axis | Moment of Inertia |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Thin Rod (Length $L$)** | Perpendicular through center | $\\frac{1}{12} M L^2$ |\n| **Thin Rod (Length $L$)** | Perpendicular through end | $\\frac{1}{3} M L^2$ |\n| **Circular Ring (Radius $R$)** | Central symmetry axis | $M R^2$ |\n| **Circular Ring (Radius $R$)** | Diameter axis | $\\frac{1}{2} M R^2$ |\n| **Circular Disc (Radius $R$)** | Central perpendicular axis | $\\frac{1}{2} M R^2$ |\n| **Circular Disc (Radius $R$)** | Diameter axis | $\\frac{1}{4} M R^2$ |\n| **Solid Cylinder / Disc** | Longitudinal central axis | $\\frac{1}{2} M R^2$ |\n| **Solid Sphere (Radius $R$)** | Any diameter axis | $\\frac{2}{5} M R^2$ |\n| **Hollow Sphere (Thin shell)**| Any diameter axis | $\\frac{2}{3} M R^2$ |\n\n### 5.3 Angular Momentum & Torque\n- **Torque:** $$\\vec{\\tau} = \\vec{r} \\times \\vec{F} = \\frac{d\\vec{L}}{dt}$$\n- **Angular Momentum of Rigid Body:**\n  $$\\vec{L} = \\vec{r}_{cm} \\times M\\vec{v}_{cm} + I_{cm}\\vec{\\omega}$$\n- **Conservation of Angular Momentum:**\n  $$\\text{If } \\vec{\\tau}_{\\text{ext}} = 0 \\implies \\vec{L}_{\\text{initial}} = \\vec{L}_{\\text{final}}$$\n\n---\n\n## 6. Rolling Motion on Incline\n\nFor a symmetric body with radius $R$, mass $M$, and $I_{cm} = \\beta M R^2$ rolling down an incline $\\theta$ without slipping:\n- **Linear Acceleration:**\n  $$a_{cm} = \\frac{g\\sin\\theta}{1 + \\frac{I_{cm}}{MR^2}} = \\frac{g\\sin\\theta}{1 + \\beta}$$\n- **Friction Force:**\n  $$f = \\frac{Mg\\sin\\theta}{1 + \\frac{MR^2}{I_{cm}}} = \\frac{\\beta}{1 + \\beta} Mg\\sin\\theta$$\n- **Minimum Coefficient of Static Friction for Pure Rolling:**\n  $$\\mu_s \\ge \\frac{\\beta}{1 + \\beta} \\tan\\theta$$\n- **Linear Velocity at Bottom of Height $h$:**\n  $$v_{cm} = \\sqrt{\\frac{2gh}{1 + \\beta}}$$\n"
