    "content": "# Electrodynamics, Magnetism & EMI \u2014 High-Yield Formula Sheet\n*Curated by Nelov Mallick (IIT Delhi) \u00b7 Authentic JEE Advanced Revision*\n\n---\n\n## 1. Electrostatics & Gauss's Law\n\n### 1.1 Coulomb's Force & Electric Field\n- **Coulomb's Law:** $$\\vec{F} = \\frac{1}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_0} \\frac{q_1 q_2}{r^2}\\hat{r}$$\n- **Field of a Uniformly Charged Ring on its Axis:**\n  $$E(x) = \\frac{1}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_0}\\frac{Q x}{(R^2 + x^2)^{3/2}}$$\n  $$\\text{Maximum Field occurs at } x = \\frac{R}{\\sqrt{2}} \\implies E_{\\max} = \\frac{Q}{6\\sqrt{3}\\pi\\varepsilon_0 R^2}$$\n- **Infinite Uniform Wire:** $$E = \\frac{\\lambda}{2\\pi\\varepsilon_0 r}$$\n- **Uniformly Charged Infinite Sheet:** $$E = \\frac{\\sigma}{2\\varepsilon_0}$$ (independent of distance)\n- **Conducting Surface Field:** $$E = \\frac{\\sigma}{\\varepsilon_0}$$ (directed perpendicularly outwards)\n\n### 1.2 Electric Dipole\n- **Dipole Moment:** $$\\vec{p} = q(2\\vec{a})$$ (from negative to positive charge)\n- **Axial Field ($r \\gg a$):** $$\\vec{E}_{\\text{axial}} = \\frac{2k\\vec{p}}{r^3}$$\n- **Equatorial Field ($r \\gg a$):** $$\\vec{E}_{\\text{equatorial}} = -\\frac{k\\vec{p}}{r^3}$$\n- **Torque & Potential Energy in External Uniform Field:**\n  $$\\vec{\\tau} = \\vec{p} \\times \\vec{E}, \\quad U = -\\vec{p}\\cdot\\vec{E}$$\n- **Force on Dipole in Non-Uniform Field:**\n  $$\\vec{F} = (\\vec{p}\\cdot\\nabla)\\vec{E} = p\\frac{\\partial E}{\\partial x}\\hat{i}$$ (for 1D gradient)\n\n### 1.3 Gauss's Law\n$$\\Phi_E = \\oint \\vec{E}\\cdot d\\vec{A} = \\frac{Q_{\\text{enclosed}}}{\\varepsilon_0}$$\n- **Uniform Solid Dielectric Sphere of Radius $R$ and Total Charge $Q$:**\n  $$E(r) = \\frac{Q r}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_0 R^3} \\quad (r \\le R), \\qquad E(r) = \\frac{Q}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_0 r^2} \\quad (r \\ge R)$$\n\n---\n\n## 2. Capacitance & Energy\n\n- **Parallel Plate Capacitor:** $$C_0 = \\frac{\\varepsilon_0 A}{d}$$\n- **With Dielectric Slab of thickness $t < d$ and constant $\\kappa$:**\n  $$C = \\frac{\\varepsilon_0 A}{d - t + \\frac{t}{\\kappa}}$$\n- **Stored Energy:**\n  $$U = \\frac{1}{2} C V^2 = \\frac{Q^2}{2C} = \\frac{1}{2} Q V$$\n- **Electrostatic Pressure & Attractive Plate Force:**\n  $$P_e = \\frac{1}{2}\\varepsilon_0 E^2 = \\frac{\\sigma^2}{2\\varepsilon_0}, \\quad F = P_e A = \\frac{Q^2}{2\\varepsilon_0 A}$$\n- **Charging of RC Circuit:**\n  $$q(t) = C\\mathcal{E}\\left(1 - e^{-t / RC}\\right), \\quad I(t) = \\frac{\\mathcal{E}}{R} e^{-t / RC}$$\n- **Discharging of RC Circuit:**\n  $$q(t) = Q_0 e^{-t / RC}, \\quad I(t) = \\frac{Q_0}{RC} e^{-t / RC}$$\n\n---\n\n## 3. Current Electricity & Circuits\n\n- **Drift Velocity & Current Density:**\n  $$v_d = \\frac{e E \\tau}{m}, \\quad I = n e A v_d, \\quad \\vec{j} = n e \\vec{v}_d = \\sigma \\vec{E}$$\n- **Resistivity & Temperature Dependence:**\n  $$\\rho = \\frac{m}{n e^2 \\tau}, \\quad \\rho(T) = \\rho_0 [1 + \\alpha (T - T_0)]$$\n- **Color Coding Resistance:** `BBROYGBVGW` (Black, Brown, Red, Orange, Yellow, Green, Blue, Violet, Grey, White)\n- **Internal Resistance & Maximum Power Transfer Theorem:**\n  $$I = \\frac{\\mathcal{E}}{R + r}, \\quad V_{\\text{terminal}} = \\mathcal{E} - Ir$$\n  $$\\text{Maximum power delivered to load occurs when } R_{\\text{load}} = r_{\\text{internal}} \\implies P_{\\max} = \\frac{\\mathcal{E}^2}{4r}$$\n\n---\n\n## 4. Magnetism & Ampere's Law\n\n- **Biot-Savart Law:**\n  $$d\\vec{B} = \\frac{\\mu_0}{4\\pi} \\frac{I(d\\vec{\\ell} \\times \\hat{r})}{r^2}$$\n- **Long Straight Wire:** $$B = \\frac{\\mu_0 I}{2\\pi r}$$\n- **Center of Circular Coil ($N$ turns):** $$B = \\frac{\\mu_0 N I}{2 R}$$\n- **Axis of Circular Coil at distance $x$:**\n  $$B(x) = \\frac{\\mu_0 N I R^2}{2(R^2 + x^2)^{3/2}}$$\n- **Ampere's Circuital Law:**\n  $$\\oint \\vec{B}\\cdot d\\vec{\\ell} = \\mu_0 I_{\\text{enclosed}}$$\n- **Ideal Solenoid:** $$B = \\mu_0 n I$$ ($n = N/L$)\n- **Ideal Toroid:** $$B = \\frac{\\mu_0 N I}{2\\pi r}$$\n- **Lorentz Force:**\n  $$\\vec{F} = q(\\vec{E} + \\vec{v} \\times \\vec{B})$$\n- **Charged Particle in Uniform $\\vec{B}$ ($\\vec{v} \\perp \\vec{B}$):**\n  $$r = \\frac{mv}{qB} = \\frac{p}{qB} = \\frac{\\sqrt{2mK}}{qB}, \\quad \\mathcal{T} = \\frac{2\\pi m}{qB}, \\quad \\text{Pitch } p = v_\\parallel \\mathcal{T} = \\frac{2\\pi m v \\cos\\theta}{qB}$$\n\n---\n\n## 5. Electromagnetic Induction & AC Circuits\n\n- **Magnetic Flux:** $$\\Phi_B = \\iint \\vec{B}\\cdot d\\vec{A}$$\n- **Faraday's Law:** $$\\mathcal{E} = -\\frac{d\\Phi_B}{dt}$$\n- **Motional EMF in Straight Conductor:** $$\\mathcal{E} = (\\vec{v} \\times \\vec{B})\\cdot\\vec{\\ell}$$\n- **Rotating Rod of length $L$ in uniform $\\vec{B}$:**\n  $$\\mathcal{E} = \\frac{1}{2} B \\omega L^2$$\n- **Self & Mutual Inductance:**\n  $$\\Phi_B = L I \\implies \\mathcal{E}_L = -L\\frac{dI}{dt}, \\quad U_L = \\frac{1}{2} L I^2$$\n  $$\\text{Coupling Coefficient: } M = k\\sqrt{L_1 L_2} \\quad (0 \\le k \\le 1)$$\n- **Growth in LR Circuit:**\n  $$I(t) = \\frac{\\mathcal{E}}{R}\\left(1 - e^{-t / \\tau_L}\\right), \\quad \\tau_L = \\frac{L}{R}$$\n- **Series LCR Circuit & Resonance:**\n  $$Z = \\sqrt{R^2 + (\\omega L - \\frac{1}{\\omega C})^2}, \\quad \\tan\\phi = \\frac{\\omega L - \\frac{1}{\\omega C}}{R}$$\n  $$\\text{Resonant Frequency: } \\omega_0 = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{LC}} \\implies f_0 = \\frac{1}{2\\pi\\sqrt{LC}}$$\n  $$\\text{Quality Factor } Q = \\frac{\\omega_0 L}{R} = \\frac{1}{\\omega_0 C R} = \\frac{1}{R}\\sqrt{\\frac{L}{C}}$$\n"
