    "content": "# Master Calculus \u2014 Differential & Integral Formula Sheet\n*Curated by Nelov Mallick (IIT Delhi) \u00b7 Authentic JEE Advanced Revision*\n\n---\n\n## 1. Limits, Continuity & Differentiability\n\n### 1.1 Standard Limits\n- $$\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\sin x}{x} = 1, \\quad \\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\tan x}{x} = 1, \\quad \\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{1 - \\cos x}{x^2} = \\frac{1}{2}$$\n- $$\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{e^x - 1}{x} = 1, \\quad \\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{a^x - 1}{x} = \\ln a, \\quad \\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\ln(1 + x)}{x} = 1$$\n- **$1^\\infty$ Indeterminate Form:**\n  $$\\text{If } \\lim_{x\\to a} f(x) = 1 \\text{ and } \\lim_{x\\to a} g(x) = \\infty \\implies \\lim_{x\\to a} [f(x)]^{g(x)} = e^{\\lim_{x\\to a} g(x)[f(x) - 1]}$$\n\n### 1.2 Differentiability Criteria\nA function $f(x)$ is differentiable at $x = c$ iff left-hand derivative equals right-hand derivative:\n$$f'(c^-) = \\lim_{h\\to 0^+} \\frac{f(c) - f(c - h)}{h} = \\lim_{h\\to 0^+} \\frac{f(c + h) - f(c)}{h} = f'(c^+)$$\n- Differentiability strictly implies continuity, but continuity does NOT imply differentiability (e.g., $f(x) = |x|$ at $x=0$).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Differential Calculus & Applications of Derivatives\n\n### 2.1 Mean Value Theorems\n- **Rolle's Theorem:** If $f(x)$ is continuous on $[a, b]$, differentiable on $(a, b)$, and $f(a) = f(b)$, then $\\exists c \\in (a, b)$ such that $f'(c) = 0$.\n- **Lagrange's Mean Value Theorem (LMVT):** If $f(x)$ is continuous on $[a, b]$ and differentiable on $(a, b)$, then $\\exists c \\in (a, b)$ such that:\n  $$f'(c) = \\frac{f(b) - f(a)}{b - a}$$\n\n### 2.2 Tangents & Normals\n- Equation of tangent at $(x_1, y_1)$: $$y - y_1 = m(x - x_1), \\quad m = \\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{(x_1, y_1)}$$\n- Equation of normal at $(x_1, y_1)$: $$y - y_1 = -\\frac{1}{m}(x - x_1)$$\n- **Length of Subtangent & Subnormal:**\n  $$\\text{Length of Subtangent} = \\left|\\frac{y_1}{m}\\right|, \\quad \\text{Length of Subnormal} = |y_1 m|$$\n\n---\n\n## 3. Indefinite & Definite Integrals\n\n### 3.1 Standard Algebraic & Trigonometric Forms\n- $$\\int \\frac{dx}{x^2 + a^2} = \\frac{1}{a}\\arctan\\left(\\frac{x}{a}\\right) + C$$\n- $$\\int \\frac{dx}{x^2 - a^2} = \\frac{1}{2a}\\ln\\left|\\frac{x - a}{x + a}\\right| + C$$\n- $$\\int \\frac{dx}{\\sqrt{a^2 - x^2}} = \\arcsin\\left(\\frac{x}{a}\\right) + C$$\n- $$\\int \\frac{dx}{\\sqrt{x^2 \\pm a^2}} = \\ln\\left|x + \\sqrt{x^2 \\pm a^2}\\right| + C$$\n- $$\\int \\sqrt{a^2 - x^2}\\,dx = \\frac{x}{2}\\sqrt{a^2 - x^2} + \\frac{a^2}{2}\\arcsin\\left(\\frac{x}{a}\\right) + C$$\n- **Integration by Parts:**\n  $$\\int u v\\,dx = u\\int v\\,dx - \\int \\left(u'\\int v\\,dx\\right)dx \\quad (\\text{ILATE rule})$$\n\n### 3.2 Core Definite Integral Properties\n- **King's Property:**\n  $$\\int_a^b f(x)\\,dx = \\int_a^b f(a + b - x)\\,dx$$\n- **Queen's Property:**\n  $$\\int_0^{2a} f(x)\\,dx = \\int_0^a f(x)\\,dx + \\int_0^a f(2a - x)\\,dx = \\begin{cases} 2\\int_0^a f(x)\\,dx & \\text{if } f(2a - x) = f(x) \\\\ 0 & \\text{if } f(2a - x) = -f(x) \\end{cases}$$\n- **Even/Odd Functions:**\n  $$\\int_{-a}^a f(x)\\,dx = \\begin{cases} 2\\int_0^a f(x)\\,dx & \\text{if } f(-x) = f(x) \\text{ (Even)} \\\\ 0 & \\text{if } f(-x) = -f(x) \\text{ (Odd)} \\end{cases}$$\n- **Periodic Function Integral ($f(x + T) = f(x)$):**\n  $$\\int_0^{nT} f(x)\\,dx = n\\int_0^T f(x)\\,dx, \\quad \\int_a^{a + nT} f(x)\\,dx = n\\int_0^T f(x)\\,dx$$\n\n### 3.3 Leibniz's Rule for Differentiating Under the Integral Sign\n$$\\frac{d}{dx}\\left[\\int_{\\phi(x)}^{\\psi(x)} f(t, x)\\,dt\\right] = f(\\psi(x), x)\\cdot\\psi'(x) - f(\\phi(x), x)\\cdot\\phi'(x) + \\int_{\\phi(x)}^{\\psi(x)} \\frac{\\partial f(t, x)}{\\partial x}\\,dt$$\n\n---\n\n## 4. Differential Equations\n\n- **Variable Separable Form:** $$f(x)\\,dx = g(y)\\,dy \\implies \\int f(x)\\,dx = \\int g(y)\\,dy + C$$\n- **Homogeneous Form:** $$\\frac{dy}{dx} = f\\left(\\frac{y}{x}\\right) \\implies \\text{substitute } y = vx$$\n- **First Order Linear Differential Equation (Leibniz Equation):**\n  $$\\frac{dy}{dx} + P(x) y = Q(x)$$\n  $$\\text{Integrating Factor (IF)} = e^{\\int P(x)\\,dx}$$\n  $$\\text{General Solution: } y \\cdot (\\text{IF}) = \\int Q(x)\\cdot(\\text{IF})\\,dx + C$$\n- **Exact Differential Shortcuts:**\n  - $d(xy) = x\\,dy + y\\,dx$\n  - $d\\left(\\frac{y}{x}\\right) = \\frac{x\\,dy - y\\,dx}{x^2}$\n  - $d\\left(\\frac{x}{y}\\right) = \\frac{y\\,dx - x\\,dy}{y^2}$\n  - $d\\left(\\arctan\\frac{y}{x}\\right) = \\frac{x\\,dy - y\\,dx}{x^2 + y^2}$\n  - $d\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\ln(x^2 + y^2)\\right) = \\frac{x\\,dx + y\\,dy}{x^2 + y^2}$\n"
