    "content": "# Coordinate Geometry & Conic Sections \u2014 High-Yield Formula Sheet\n*Curated by Nelov Mallick (IIT Delhi) \u00b7 Authentic JEE Advanced Revision*\n\n---\n\n## 1. Straight Lines & Circles\n\n### 1.1 Straight Lines\n- **Perpendicular Distance from $(x_1, y_1)$ to $ax + by + c = 0$:**\n  $$d = \\frac{|a x_1 + b y_1 + c|}{\\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}}$$\n- **Distance Between Parallel Lines $ax + by + c_1 = 0$ and $ax + by + c_2 = 0$:**\n  $$d = \\frac{|c_1 - c_2|}{\\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}}$$\n- **Angle Bisectors:**\n  $$\\frac{a_1 x + b_1 y + c_1}{\\sqrt{a_1^2 + b_1^2}} = \\pm \\frac{a_2 x + b_2 y + c_2}{\\sqrt{a_2^2 + b_2^2}}$$\n\n### 1.2 Circles\n- **General Form:** $$x^2 + y^2 + 2gx + 2fy + c = 0 \\implies \\text{Center } (-g, -f), \\quad R = \\sqrt{g^2 + f^2 - c}$$\n- **Tangent at $(x_1, y_1)$ ($T=0$):**\n  $$x x_1 + y y_1 + g(x + x_1) + f(y + y_1) + c = 0$$\n- **Condition of Tangency for $y = mx + c$ with $x^2 + y^2 = a^2$:**\n  $$c^2 = a^2(1 + m^2) \\implies y = mx \\pm a\\sqrt{1 + m^2}$$\n- **Director Circle (Locus of perpendicular tangents):**\n  $$x^2 + y^2 = 2a^2$$\n\n---\n\n## 2. Parabola ($y^2 = 4ax$)\n\n- **Parameters:** Focus: $(a, 0)$, Directrix: $x = -a$, Axis: $y = 0$, Latus Rectum: $4a$.\n- **Parametric Representation:** $x = a t^2, \\quad y = 2 a t$.\n- **Tangent Equations:**\n  - Point Form: $y y_1 = 2a(x + x_1)$\n  - Parametric Form: $t y = x + a t^2$\n  - Slope Form ($m = 1/t$): $$y = m x + \\frac{a}{m}$$\n- **Normal Equations:**\n  - Parametric Form: $$y + t x = 2 a t + a t^3$$\n  - Slope Form ($m = -t$): $$y = m x - 2 a m - a m^3$$\n- **Focal Chord Properties:**\n  - If chord joining $t_1$ and $t_2$ passes through focus $(a, 0) \\implies t_1 t_2 = -1$.\n  - Length of focal chord: $$L = a\\left(t + \\frac{1}{t}\\right)^2 \\ge 4a$$\n  - Semi-latus rectum is the harmonic mean of the segments of any focal chord:\n    $$\\frac{1}{SP} + \\frac{1}{SQ} = \\frac{1}{a}$$\n\n---\n\n## 3. Ellipse ($\\frac{x^2}{a^2} + \\frac{y^2}{b^2} = 1, \\quad a > b$)\n\n- **Eccentricity ($e < 1$):**\n  $$b^2 = a^2(1 - e^2) \\implies e = \\sqrt{1 - \\frac{b^2}{a^2}}$$\n- **Foci:** $(\\pm a e, 0)$, **Directrices:** $x = \\pm \\frac{a}{e}$, **Latus Rectum:** $\\frac{2b^2}{a}$.\n- **Focal Radii Property:** For any point $P$ on ellipse:\n  $$S P + S' P = 2a \\quad (\\text{Constant})$$\n- **Parametric Coordinates:** $(a\\cos\\theta, b\\sin\\theta)$.\n- **Tangent Equations:**\n  - Point Form: $\\frac{x x_1}{a^2} + \\frac{y y_1}{b^2} = 1$\n  - Slope Form: $$y = m x \\pm \\sqrt{a^2 m^2 + b^2}$$\n- **Director Circle:**\n  $$x^2 + y^2 = a^2 + b^2$$\n\n---\n\n## 4. Hyperbola ($\\frac{x^2}{a^2} - \\frac{y^2}{b^2} = 1$)\n\n- **Eccentricity ($e > 1$):**\n  $$b^2 = a^2(e^2 - 1) \\implies e = \\sqrt{1 + \\frac{b^2}{a^2}}$$\n- **Foci:** $(\\pm a e, 0)$, **Directrices:** $x = \\pm \\frac{a}{e}$, **Latus Rectum:** $\\frac{2b^2}{a}$.\n- **Focal Radii Property:**\n  $$|S P - S' P| = 2a \\quad (\\text{Constant})$$\n- **Asymptotes:**\n  $$y = \\pm \\frac{b}{a} x \\implies \\frac{x^2}{a^2} - \\frac{y^2}{b^2} = 0$$\n  Angle between asymptotes: $2\\theta = 2\\arctan(b/a)$.\n- **Tangent in Slope Form:**\n  $$y = m x \\pm \\sqrt{a^2 m^2 - b^2}$$\n- **Director Circle:**\n  $$x^2 + y^2 = a^2 - b^2 \\quad (a > b)$$\n- **Rectangular Hyperbola ($xy = c^2$):**\n  - Eccentricity: $e = \\sqrt{2}$.\n  - Parametric Form: $(c t, c/t)$.\n  - Tangent at $t$: $$\\frac{x}{t} + y t = 2c \\implies x + y t^2 = 2c t$$\n"
