    "content": "# Matrices, Vectors & 3D Geometry \u2014 High-Yield Formula Sheet\n*Curated by Nelov Mallick (IIT Delhi) \u00b7 Authentic JEE Advanced Revision*\n\n---\n\n## 1. Matrices & Determinants\n\n### 1.1 Adjoint & Inverse Properties (Square Matrix $A$ of order $n$)\n- $$A \\cdot (\\text{adj } A) = (\\text{adj } A) \\cdot A = |A| I_n$$\n- $$|\\text{adj } A| = |A|^{n-1}$$\n- $$|\\text{adj}(\\text{adj } A)| = |A|^{(n-1)^2}$$\n- $$\\text{adj}(\\text{adj } A) = |A|^{n-2} A$$\n- $$\\text{adj}(A B) = (\\text{adj } B)(\\text{adj } A)$$\n- $$A^{-1} = \\frac{1}{|A|}\\text{adj } A \\quad (|A| \\ne 0)$$\n- $$(A^T)^{-1} = (A^{-1})^T, \\quad (A B)^{-1} = B^{-1} A^{-1}$$\n\n### 1.2 System of Linear Equations ($A X = B$)\n- **Cramer's Rule:**\n  $$x = \\frac{\\Delta_1}{\\Delta}, \\quad y = \\frac{\\Delta_2}{\\Delta}, \\quad z = \\frac{\\Delta_3}{\\Delta}$$\n  1. Unique Solution: $\\Delta \\ne 0$\n  2. Infinite Solutions (Consistent): $\\Delta = 0$ and $\\Delta_1 = \\Delta_2 = \\Delta_3 = 0$ (check rank consistency)\n  3. No Solution (Inconsistent): $\\Delta = 0$ and at least one $\\Delta_i \\ne 0$\n\n---\n\n## 2. Vector Algebra\n\n### 2.1 Dot & Cross Products\n- **Scalar (Dot) Product:**\n  $$\\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{b} = |\\vec{a}||\\vec{b}|\\cos\\theta, \\quad \\text{Projection of } \\vec{a} \\text{ on } \\vec{b} = \\frac{\\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{b}}{|\\vec{b}|}$$\n- **Vector (Cross) Product:**\n  $$\\vec{a}\\times\\vec{b} = |\\vec{a}||\\vec{b}|\\sin\\theta\\,\\hat{n}$$\n  $$\\text{Area of Parallelogram with sides } \\vec{a}, \\vec{b} = |\\vec{a}\\times\\vec{b}|$$\n  $$\\text{Area of Triangle with vertices } \\vec{a}, \\vec{b}, \\vec{c} = \\frac{1}{2}|(\\vec{b} - \\vec{a})\\times(\\vec{c} - \\vec{a})|$$\n\n### 2.2 Triple Products\n- **Scalar Triple Product (Box Product):**\n  $$[\\vec{a}\\;\\vec{b}\\;\\vec{c}] = \\vec{a}\\cdot(\\vec{b}\\times\\vec{c}) = \\begin{vmatrix} a_1 & a_2 & a_3 \\\\ b_1 & b_2 & b_3 \\\\ c_1 & c_2 & c_3 \\end{vmatrix}$$\n  - Volume of Parallelepiped formed by coterminous edges $\\vec{a}, \\vec{b}, \\vec{c} = |[\\vec{a}\\;\\vec{b}\\;\\vec{c}]|$.\n  - Coplanarity Condition: Three vectors $\\vec{a}, \\vec{b}, \\vec{c}$ are coplanar iff $[\\vec{a}\\;\\vec{b}\\;\\vec{c}] = 0$.\n  - Cyclic Permutation: $[\\vec{a}\\;\\vec{b}\\;\\vec{c}] = [\\vec{b}\\;\\vec{c}\\;\\vec{a}] = [\\vec{c}\\;\\vec{a}\\;\\vec{b}] = -[\\vec{b}\\;\\vec{a}\\;\\vec{c}]$.\n- **Vector Triple Product:**\n  $$\\vec{a}\\times(\\vec{b}\\times\\vec{c}) = (\\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{c})\\vec{b} - (\\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{b})\\vec{c} \\quad (\\text{\"BAC - CAB\" Rule})$$\n\n---\n\n## 3. 3D Coordinate Geometry\n\n### 3.1 Lines in 3D Space\n- **Vector & Cartesian Form:**\n  $$\\vec{r} = \\vec{a} + \\lambda\\vec{b} \\iff \\frac{x - x_1}{a} = \\frac{y - y_1}{b} = \\frac{z - z_1}{c}$$\n- **Shortest Distance Between Two Skew Lines:**\n  $$\\vec{r} = \\vec{a}_1 + \\lambda\\vec{b}_1 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\vec{r} = \\vec{a}_2 + \\mu\\vec{b}_2$$\n  $$d = \\frac{|(\\vec{a}_2 - \\vec{a}_1)\\cdot(\\vec{b}_1\\times\\vec{b}_2)|}{|\\vec{b}_1\\times\\vec{b}_2|}$$\n- **Condition for Coplanar Lines:**\n  $$(\\vec{a}_2 - \\vec{a}_1)\\cdot(\\vec{b}_1\\times\\vec{b}_2) = 0 \\iff \\begin{vmatrix} x_2 - x_1 & y_2 - y_1 & z_2 - z_1 \\\\ a_1 & b_1 & c_1 \\\\ a_2 & b_2 & c_2 \\end{vmatrix} = 0$$\n\n### 3.2 Planes in 3D Space\n- **Equation of Plane Passing Through $\\vec{a}$ with Normal $\\vec{n}$:**\n  $$(\\vec{r} - \\vec{a})\\cdot\\vec{n} = 0 \\iff a(x - x_1) + b(y - y_1) + c(z - z_1) = 0$$\n- **Perpendicular Distance from Point $(x_0, y_0, z_0)$ to Plane $ax + by + cz + d = 0$:**\n  $$p = \\frac{|a x_0 + b y_0 + c z_0 + d|}{\\sqrt{a^2 + b^2 + c^2}}$$\n- **Angle Between Line $\\frac{x-x_1}{a} = \\frac{y-y_1}{b} = \\frac{z-z_1}{c}$ and Plane $Ax + By + Cz + D = 0$:**\n  $$\\sin\\theta = \\frac{|A a + B b + C c|}{\\sqrt{a^2 + b^2 + c^2}\\sqrt{A^2 + B^2 + C^2}}$$\n"
